WEBVTT

00:09.843 --> 00:10.844
Bingo.

00:10.927 --> 00:13.179
They'll make fine souvenirs.

00:51.843 --> 00:55.889
<i>The once-mighty superpower,
the Holy Britannian Empire,</i>

00:55.972 --> 00:57.974
<i>which had occupied a third of the world,</i>

00:58.725 --> 01:03.313
<i>fell with its 99th Emperor,
Lelouch vi Britannia,</i>

01:03.396 --> 01:06.483
<i>ultimately marking the end
of its long history.</i>

01:07.776 --> 01:12.697
<i>Turmoil ensued, fragmenting the empire
into several smaller countries.</i>

01:12.781 --> 01:16.242
<i>However, under the leadership
of Schneizel el Britannia,</i>

01:16.326 --> 01:18.661
<i>the majority of these states came together</i>

01:18.745 --> 01:21.748
<i>under the banner
of the United Federation of Nations,</i>

01:21.831 --> 01:23.917
<i>taking a new step forward.</i>

01:24.000 --> 01:27.295
<i>Peace reigned once again.
Or so it seemed...</i>

01:40.100 --> 01:42.602
<i>Kowa Period, Year Three.</i>

01:42.685 --> 01:47.440
<i>A faction of Britannian forces declares
war on the United States of Japan</i>

01:47.524 --> 01:50.401
<i>and launch a surprise attack
on the Hokkaido Block,</i>

01:50.485 --> 01:52.821
<i>swiftly seizing control.</i>

01:52.904 --> 01:56.032
<i>There they establish
the Neo-Britannian Empire.</i>

01:57.033 --> 02:01.621
<i>And so, the Japanese people
once again faced oppression.</i>

02:01.704 --> 02:06.918
<i>Reminiscent of the days when Japan
was a territory under Britannian rule</i>

02:07.001 --> 02:09.420
<i>known as Area 11.</i>

03:43.014 --> 03:45.892
Situmpe Tower is still standing strong.

03:46.517 --> 03:48.811
Which makes that our target.

03:50.146 --> 03:52.607
Big brother,
how's the tune-up coming along?

03:52.690 --> 03:55.401
I'll need 11 more minutes.

03:56.277 --> 03:57.403
Looks like we're camping here tonight.

03:58.529 --> 04:00.490
Mmm-hmm. Looks like it.

04:06.287 --> 04:07.538
Hey, are you hungry?

04:11.084 --> 04:13.294
You really shouldn't
squirm around so much.

04:13.378 --> 04:15.922
Otherwise, who knows
what my bullets might hit.

04:17.548 --> 04:19.300
Why are you doing this to us?

04:19.384 --> 04:21.010
We're not terrorists, or collaborators!

04:21.094 --> 04:22.136
- Please!
- Every...

04:22.220 --> 04:24.764
Eleven... says...

04:24.847 --> 04:26.975
the... same... thing.

04:27.058 --> 04:28.643
I think we should drop
the whole matter, Gran.

04:28.726 --> 04:30.103
Huh?

04:30.186 --> 04:31.187
Fine.

04:34.023 --> 04:35.525
My husband!

04:36.526 --> 04:39.654
I did like you said, Greede.
I let it drop.

04:40.863 --> 04:42.573
A slight misunderstanding.

04:43.283 --> 04:44.617
Forgive us.

04:47.036 --> 04:48.204
No need to interfere.

04:51.291 --> 04:54.085
Play nice, and they walk all over you.

04:54.168 --> 04:56.629
That's the problem
with you brainless monkeys.

04:56.713 --> 04:59.090
Looks like
we'll have to teach them a lesson.

04:59.924 --> 05:01.426
So listen up!

05:01.509 --> 05:04.679
I think it's time that
you worthless Elevens learned your place!

05:05.263 --> 05:08.850
Your former Lord, Jugo Sumeragi, is dead.

05:08.933 --> 05:12.228
His daughter, Sakuya Sumeragi,
wastes away in prison!

05:13.062 --> 05:16.482
The Situmpe Wall,
which you built to keep Britannia at bay,

05:17.066 --> 05:20.695
now serves to protect
our Neo-Britannian Empire.

05:20.778 --> 05:23.156
Crushing the Black Knights'
invasion plans.

05:23.865 --> 05:26.075
Two times. Definitively.

05:26.784 --> 05:29.662
You're all livestock
trapped in the ultimate cage.

05:29.746 --> 05:31.414
There's no hope for any of you!

05:32.582 --> 05:36.461
Don't bother thinking about things.
Live your idle lives.

05:36.544 --> 05:39.630
Having human feelings
and human rights are beyond you.

05:40.465 --> 05:44.010
You should feel honored
to serve as my target practice!

05:45.553 --> 05:48.890
Security forces,
take out the rest of the trash.

05:49.390 --> 05:50.892
Yes, my lord!

05:57.648 --> 05:58.941
<i>In other news,</i>

05:59.025 --> 06:02.528
<i>security forces carried out
a counter-terrorism operation yesterday</i>

06:02.612 --> 06:05.365
<i>in the Kushiro Ghetto
of the Tsurumai District.</i>

06:05.990 --> 06:07.408
<i>The Kirkwayne Security Forces</i>

06:07.492 --> 06:09.243
<i>- reported zero casualties</i>
- Oh.

06:09.327 --> 06:11.329
<i>Meanwhile 36 Eleven terrorists</i>

06:11.412 --> 06:12.663
<i>were killed.</i>
Kirkwayne?

06:16.876 --> 06:17.877
Hi, welcome!

06:17.960 --> 06:20.546
Would you fill up the oil
and recharge the battery, please?

06:23.674 --> 06:25.176
What the hell's the matter with you?

06:25.259 --> 06:26.761
You stupid girl!

06:26.844 --> 06:31.474
A single drop of that oil is worth
more than any of you Elevens!

06:31.557 --> 06:32.850
I... I'm sorry.

06:32.934 --> 06:35.228
Sorry doesn't replace the oil ya spilled!

06:35.311 --> 06:36.979
Now get up, you... Uh--

06:39.524 --> 06:40.983
Why did you hit her?

06:41.067 --> 06:42.735
What the heck?

06:42.819 --> 06:44.487
Answer the question.

06:44.570 --> 06:47.365
I'm in charge here,
I'll treat her however the hell I--

06:47.448 --> 06:49.158
Ow...

06:49.700 --> 06:51.411
Hey, hey, come on now.

06:51.494 --> 06:52.995
That's enough, Ash.

06:53.079 --> 06:54.914
Let's all just relax
and take a breath here.

06:55.790 --> 06:58.000
Sorry about that.
My brother's such a hothead.

06:58.084 --> 06:59.544
What's wrong with you people?

06:59.627 --> 07:01.504
You know,
I've got half a mind to call the--

07:01.587 --> 07:03.548
Look, we don't want any trouble here.

07:03.631 --> 07:05.883
I'm sure you and I can come
to an understanding.

07:05.967 --> 07:07.635
Why don't we step inside
and talk this out.

07:10.263 --> 07:12.140
Can you stand?
- Huh?

07:12.223 --> 07:13.516
- Let me help.
- Oh...

07:14.767 --> 07:15.768
I'm sorry.

07:17.395 --> 07:19.897
Is your brother going to be
all right by himself?

07:20.481 --> 07:21.607
Yeah.

07:23.192 --> 07:24.569
You don't have to worry about him.

07:26.237 --> 07:28.030
I was outta line before.

07:28.114 --> 07:30.992
Are ya hurt?
If you're tired, you can rest inside.

07:31.075 --> 07:34.454
After all, you Japanese
are a national treasure to us.

07:34.537 --> 07:35.538
Um, thank you.

07:36.038 --> 07:39.834
Well, please allow me to pay restitution
for how I've treated you.

07:39.917 --> 07:41.252
And overtime, of course.

07:41.961 --> 07:43.087
Just a minute!

07:43.171 --> 07:46.257
You rest. I'll take care of this one.

07:46.340 --> 07:47.800
You're a treasure, I tell ya!

07:47.884 --> 07:50.219
Welcome, what can I get you?

07:50.303 --> 07:54.265
He had a change of heart after our talk.
I don't think he's such a bad guy.

07:55.600 --> 07:57.268
Are you, like, a magician?

07:57.977 --> 08:00.438
So I'm a magician, huh? Sounds nice!

08:04.692 --> 08:05.693
SEVEN SHINING STARS, OTARU HIDEOUT

08:05.776 --> 08:06.777
I don't like it!

08:06.861 --> 08:09.655
Do you honestly expect us
to rely on complete strangers?

08:09.739 --> 08:11.324
They've got a great track record.

08:11.407 --> 08:14.035
There was the Kutchan
Cricket Stadium Attack, for one.

08:14.118 --> 08:16.829
The Rarumanaino Dam Eniwa Murder.

08:16.913 --> 08:19.624
And The Niseko Panorama Line Attack.
Isn't that right?

08:19.707 --> 08:20.708
Mmm.

08:20.791 --> 08:24.170
They seem to be taking down
Britannian officials in each case,

08:24.253 --> 08:26.380
while saving Japanese lives.

08:26.464 --> 08:28.299
The Nameless Mercenaries, right?

08:28.382 --> 08:31.010
Yeah. Just showed up out of nowhere
about a year ago.

08:32.386 --> 08:34.555
<i>All we know about them
is that they're brothers.</i>

08:34.639 --> 08:35.723
<i>And Britannian.</i>

08:36.474 --> 08:38.267
No way! I can't trust these guys.

08:38.976 --> 08:40.061
I have to agree.

08:40.144 --> 08:42.188
I'd hate for us to put our faith
in these two

08:42.271 --> 08:43.856
just to get stabbed in the back.

08:43.940 --> 08:46.484
But if the rumors about them are true,
it's worth considering.

08:47.235 --> 08:49.070
<i>They would make formidable allies.</i>

08:51.906 --> 08:53.157
More cats?

08:53.950 --> 08:55.826
The poor things
were floating down the river.

08:56.327 --> 08:57.787
I almost didn't get there in time.

08:58.955 --> 09:00.331
They're so cute!

09:03.834 --> 09:06.754
Wait, are you seriously thinking
about taking in more strays?

09:07.338 --> 09:09.131
I'll look after them.
You're joking, right?

09:09.215 --> 09:10.841
I'm the one who takes care of them.

09:10.925 --> 09:12.510
All you do is buy their food.

09:13.928 --> 09:16.138
That wasn't a "no," right?
Huh?

09:16.764 --> 09:19.183
It's your lucky day, little ones.
Welcome to the family.

09:19.267 --> 09:20.935
We never agreed on that.

09:21.018 --> 09:22.603
Would you rather
I throw them back in?

09:22.687 --> 09:24.480
Oh, sure, make me the bad guy.

09:24.564 --> 09:25.606
Then I guess it's settled.

09:25.690 --> 09:27.858
Ash! Are you serious?

09:30.653 --> 09:31.821
I wonder

09:31.904 --> 09:32.947
if they're from the same litter?

09:33.030 --> 09:34.031
Probably.

09:34.657 --> 09:36.534
All right,
they're registered for adoption.

09:38.035 --> 09:40.329
I just hope that they both
end up in a good home.

09:40.871 --> 09:41.872
So do I.

09:41.956 --> 09:45.042
If you keep this up,
the trailer's gonna be full of strays.

09:45.126 --> 09:47.169
Maybe we should change careers
and open up a pet shop.

09:47.878 --> 09:49.297
I'll let you handle running it.

09:49.922 --> 09:51.132
I'd be useless.

09:51.215 --> 09:53.301
Well, you could do it
if you just tried!

09:55.595 --> 09:58.598
Hmm, not a bad set up.

09:58.681 --> 10:00.474
This might be fun after all.

10:00.850 --> 10:02.143
Sorry to disappoint you.

10:02.685 --> 10:04.145
But the theater's closed.

10:04.729 --> 10:06.897
I heard this place had some great films.

10:06.981 --> 10:09.233
Been years since
this place screened something.

10:09.317 --> 10:10.651
We got an invite.

10:10.735 --> 10:14.155
The film code was 946W465.

10:16.115 --> 10:18.159
I invited you. Call me Black Cat.

10:18.242 --> 10:20.036
Pleasure to meet you.

10:20.119 --> 10:22.079
I'm Rozé, and this is Ash.

10:22.788 --> 10:24.290
We can talk more inside.

10:25.374 --> 10:26.626
So, what do you think?

10:27.209 --> 10:28.669
I don't sense any hostility.

10:28.753 --> 10:29.962
Then let's go.

10:33.382 --> 10:36.969
This is Greede Kirkwayne,
one of the Einbergs in charge of strategy.

10:38.137 --> 10:41.557
His younger brother, Gran Kirkwayne.
Also with the Einbergs.

10:41.641 --> 10:45.186
He's a captain of this territory's
Knightmare Frame Combat Forces.

10:46.187 --> 10:47.229
They claim to be conducting

10:47.313 --> 10:50.191
security operations
and counter-terrorism activities,

10:50.274 --> 10:51.525
but that's a lie.

10:51.609 --> 10:53.819
They've killed countless Japanese
just for fun.

10:56.447 --> 10:58.908
Two years ago, they murdered my family.

10:59.450 --> 11:02.495
There are so many of us
who have suffered at their hands.

11:02.578 --> 11:04.705
We want to hire the two of you
to take them out.

11:05.790 --> 11:06.791
What do you think, Ash?

11:07.708 --> 11:09.001
It's up to you.

11:09.085 --> 11:11.504
Whatever you decide to do,
I'll follow your lead.

11:12.713 --> 11:13.964
Will you take the job?

11:15.966 --> 11:18.219
We'd be taking on two of the Einbergs.

11:18.302 --> 11:20.888
Key figures in Neo-Britannia's military.

11:21.472 --> 11:23.099
Fighting them won't be a walk in the park.

11:23.766 --> 11:26.477
Just that makes the whole idea
sound worthwhile.

11:26.560 --> 11:27.561
Then...

11:27.645 --> 11:30.439
Yeah, we've got it covered.
My brother and I are on the job.

11:32.650 --> 11:34.485
KIRKWAYNE DOMAIN

11:35.778 --> 11:38.823
<i>We've received the transmission
from the nearby police force.</i>

11:38.906 --> 11:41.075
<i>The Japanese terrorist group
has gone silent.</i>

11:41.158 --> 11:42.493
<i>The area is clear.</i>

11:43.077 --> 11:44.537
Yeah, yeah. Understood.

11:45.246 --> 11:47.498
What a pathetic excuse for a police force.

11:48.124 --> 11:50.710
<i>Can't even handle
a few Elevens on their own.</i>

11:50.793 --> 11:52.712
That's exactly why we're here.

11:52.795 --> 11:55.423
And besides, Lord Norland
will be quite pleased with us

11:55.506 --> 11:57.174
after if we take them out ourselves.

11:57.258 --> 11:59.051
<i>Fair enough.</i>

11:59.135 --> 12:00.219
<i>Captain Gran, up ahead...</i>

12:00.302 --> 12:01.303
Hmm?

12:01.387 --> 12:02.763
<i>Huh? The hell is that?</i>

12:02.847 --> 12:05.057
What's going on?
Put in on-screen.

12:05.141 --> 12:06.142
<i>Yes, sir.</i>

12:06.767 --> 12:07.768
<i>Investigate it.</i>

12:07.852 --> 12:08.853
<i>Yes, sir.</i>

12:17.319 --> 12:19.405
Come one, come all!

12:19.488 --> 12:22.616
Members of the Kirkwayne Security Force!

12:22.700 --> 12:26.245
Welcome to our humble show,
prepared just for you.

12:26.871 --> 12:29.081
I've never seen
a Knightmare Frame like that.

12:29.165 --> 12:30.166
Who are they?

12:30.249 --> 12:31.834
Go check it out!
<i>Yes, sir.</i>

12:32.501 --> 12:34.003
<i>Identify yourselves!</i>

12:34.086 --> 12:36.964
Do you actually think
we're just gonna blurt it out?

12:37.798 --> 12:39.925
Very well, if you insist.

12:40.009 --> 12:41.719
The two of us...

12:41.802 --> 12:44.346
are the Nameless Mercenaries!

12:49.477 --> 12:50.478
Your time is up!

12:51.562 --> 12:52.772
We're gonna crush you!

12:57.735 --> 12:59.278
<i>The Nameless Mercenaries?</i>

12:59.361 --> 13:00.529
<i>I've heard of them.</i>

13:00.613 --> 13:02.114
<i>A pair of Britannian brothers</i>

13:02.198 --> 13:05.910
<i>who engage in terrorist activities
at the behest of Elevens.</i>

13:05.993 --> 13:08.621
You've killed
way too many Japanese citizens.

13:08.704 --> 13:10.372
That's why we took on this request.

13:10.456 --> 13:11.665
We're here to finish you off.

13:12.249 --> 13:13.250
You what?

13:13.334 --> 13:15.002
You really think you can?

13:15.085 --> 13:17.046
You really think we can't?

13:23.594 --> 13:24.595
They vanished.

13:25.304 --> 13:26.305
<i>That's impossible!</i>

13:26.806 --> 13:28.265
<i>Fire!
Yes, sir!</i>

13:37.233 --> 13:39.401
Without taking a step? You're kidding.

13:40.152 --> 13:42.947
Units 2 and 3,
attack the infiltrating Knightmare Frame.

13:43.030 --> 13:45.115
Security forces, search for the brat.

13:45.199 --> 13:48.035
<i>Greede, I'll jump in too.</i>
- Very well.

13:48.118 --> 13:51.455
Show that Knightmare what happens
to those who defy the Kirkwaynes.

13:56.877 --> 13:59.630
We've never even been
able to get this close before.

14:04.510 --> 14:05.678
But those two...

14:06.428 --> 14:07.638
they might...

14:12.643 --> 14:14.895
I've secured your route
to the main stronghold.

14:15.521 --> 14:16.605
Thank you, Ash.

14:17.273 --> 14:19.233
Now just stick to the plan.

14:19.316 --> 14:20.317
<i>Understood.</i>

14:22.403 --> 14:25.281
Units 2 and 3,
spread out and contain the target.

14:25.364 --> 14:28.742
Hey, now. Save some for me, will ya?

14:28.826 --> 14:31.871
<i>Vanguard units!
Just try to put some pressure on him.</i>

14:32.580 --> 14:34.081
<i>Let me handle the fun part.</i>

14:36.542 --> 14:38.043
<i>Unit 2, engage.</i>

14:39.128 --> 14:40.963
<i>Unit 3, surround Point B15.</i>

14:42.298 --> 14:44.133
<i>Unit 2, continue suppressive fire.</i>

14:56.437 --> 14:57.438
Stay alert.

14:57.521 --> 14:59.398
This enemy is a capable pilot.

14:59.481 --> 15:01.775
Coming from you,
that's quite the compliment.

15:02.276 --> 15:03.277
Looking for this?

15:03.819 --> 15:04.820
Pretty careless of you

15:04.904 --> 15:06.864
when there are reports
of an intruder around.

15:06.947 --> 15:08.449
Security, to my office.

15:08.532 --> 15:09.533
No one's coming.

15:10.159 --> 15:12.036
After they led me to the armory,

15:12.119 --> 15:13.120
I told them it was nap time,

15:13.203 --> 15:15.164
and they all fell asleep
right on the spot.

15:15.873 --> 15:17.291
Now, down to business...

15:18.834 --> 15:20.502
Are you going to kill me?

15:20.586 --> 15:23.380
Hmm. You like playing chess, right?

15:23.923 --> 15:26.175
How about we play a strategy game,
you and me?

15:27.092 --> 15:28.093
Something different,

15:28.177 --> 15:30.512
where we use Knightmare Frames
instead of chess pieces.

15:30.596 --> 15:33.223
If you win, I'll let you
and your brother off the hook.

15:33.307 --> 15:35.768
You're certainly brave,
I'll give you that.

15:36.518 --> 15:38.187
Very well, I accept.

15:38.979 --> 15:42.399
<i>Bro, sync your map
to channel Bravo One.</i>

15:42.483 --> 15:44.151
<i>I'll give you instructions from there.</i>

15:44.234 --> 15:45.235
Understood.

16:05.589 --> 16:07.174
When did you set traps?

16:07.257 --> 16:10.052
Wait, did you really think
we were gonna set up an ambush,

16:10.135 --> 16:11.261
then just wing it?

16:11.345 --> 16:13.555
<i>- So, what's our next move?</i>
- Hold.

16:14.556 --> 16:16.684
<i>We have the advantage in firepower.</i>

16:16.767 --> 16:18.435
<i>Time to go all in.</i>

16:24.066 --> 16:26.819
Hmm. You're gonna push forward?

16:26.902 --> 16:29.196
Looks like you've nowhere left to run.

16:29.279 --> 16:30.990
<i>What's your next move?</i>

16:32.700 --> 16:33.701
Let me guess.

16:33.784 --> 16:35.995
You think this is checkmate
because you've got me cornered.

16:36.078 --> 16:37.871
- Hmm?
- Of course you do.

16:37.955 --> 16:40.499
Because that's exactly
what I wanted you to think.

16:40.582 --> 16:43.752
Why don't you win first.
Then you can boast.

16:43.836 --> 16:44.837
Fair enough.

16:47.381 --> 16:49.925
Hey, bro! Time for checkmate.

16:50.009 --> 16:51.010
Copy that.

17:03.397 --> 17:04.606
<i>Fire.</i>

17:39.475 --> 17:41.101
<i>It's closing in fast!</i>

17:41.185 --> 17:42.186
<i>You bastard!</i>

17:42.269 --> 17:43.353
<i>Captain--</i>

17:47.399 --> 17:49.026
<i>It's just you and me.</i>

17:49.109 --> 17:50.527
<i>There's nowhere to run.</i>

17:52.988 --> 17:54.531
<i>Don't underestimate me.</i>

17:54.615 --> 17:56.283
<i>I am Gran Kirkwayne.</i>

17:56.366 --> 17:58.243
<i>I am an Einberg!</i>

17:58.327 --> 18:00.746
<i>Some peasant of no name
will not defeat me!</i>

18:01.371 --> 18:05.375
<i>Your idea of a fight is
to torment others from a safe distance.</i>

18:05.459 --> 18:07.836
<i>If you had known pain
and built experience,</i>

18:07.920 --> 18:09.338
<i>it would've made you stronger.</i>

18:11.590 --> 18:13.425
<i>But I guess, now we'll never know.</i>

18:14.176 --> 18:15.219
<i>Shut your mouth!</i>

18:37.324 --> 18:38.408
And checkmate.

18:39.159 --> 18:40.619
It's really a shame.

18:40.702 --> 18:41.703
Damn it!

18:42.162 --> 18:45.415
Guess that means... it's your turn now.

18:45.499 --> 18:47.751
Have you thought this through?

18:47.835 --> 18:51.713
All you're doing is branding yourselves
Neo-Britannian enemies.

18:51.797 --> 18:55.425
I can assure you that Lord Norland
will hunt you down and crush you both.

18:55.509 --> 18:57.052
And what if he does?

18:59.721 --> 19:00.764
This...

19:01.557 --> 19:02.599
is my resolve.

19:14.862 --> 19:16.864
Sakuya Sumeragi?

19:16.947 --> 19:19.700
No! You were imprisoned at Abashiri.

19:19.783 --> 19:21.827
Straight from an Einberg's mouth.

19:22.411 --> 19:24.705
Thank you. For all of your help.

19:27.791 --> 19:30.127
I haven't forgotten the Kirkwayne family.

19:30.210 --> 19:32.838
You were trusted aides to my mother,
Sherry me Britannia.

19:32.921 --> 19:35.048
You even relocated with us to Hokkaido.

19:36.133 --> 19:37.718
<i>But I was always aware of the disdain</i>

19:37.801 --> 19:39.803
<i>you and your brother had for the Japanese.</i>

19:41.638 --> 19:44.266
<i>I was also aware
that under Britannian rule,</i>

19:44.349 --> 19:47.186
<i>you and your brother abused your power
over the Japanese people.</i>

19:47.936 --> 19:52.149
<i>And when Neo-Britannia invaded this land,
you colluded with them from within.</i>

19:52.774 --> 19:55.194
<i>Not only that,
you even defected to the enemy</i>

19:55.277 --> 19:57.946
<i>and proceeded to hunt down
Sakura and I that day,</i>

19:58.739 --> 20:00.365
<i>and you are the reason
we were split apart.</i>

20:02.201 --> 20:06.038
If you really
are Sakuya Sumeragi as you claim,

20:06.121 --> 20:08.498
it appears that we've imprisoned
a worthless decoy.

20:08.582 --> 20:09.583
You're wrong.

20:10.709 --> 20:11.835
She's my friend.

20:12.377 --> 20:14.004
I tire of this game.

20:14.087 --> 20:17.883
- End this and kill me already.
- I'm going to give you a choice.

20:19.968 --> 20:23.055
What's this? Handing yourself
to me on a silver platter?

20:28.685 --> 20:30.896
I, Sakuya Sumeragi, command you!

20:30.979 --> 20:34.066
Swear to me that you will save 100 times

20:34.149 --> 20:36.151
the number of Japanese
that you have killed,

20:36.235 --> 20:37.236
and you live.

20:37.861 --> 20:39.905
If you refuse, you die.

20:50.791 --> 20:53.210
Stupid girl! One hundred times?

20:53.293 --> 20:54.461
All I have to do is pull this--

21:05.847 --> 21:07.474
<i>Ash, it's done.</i>

21:07.557 --> 21:08.558
<i>Understood.</i>

21:17.067 --> 21:19.736
Well, I think it's safe to say
we did as we promised.

21:20.487 --> 21:21.989
So think you can trust us now?

21:22.072 --> 21:25.158
You are the leader of Hokkaido's
largest resistance group,

21:25.242 --> 21:26.451
the Seven Shining Stars,

21:26.535 --> 21:27.786
right, Haruka Rutaka?

21:27.869 --> 21:29.830
Uh... how did you find out?

21:29.913 --> 21:33.000
You really shouldn't underestimate
our intelligence network.

21:33.083 --> 21:34.459
That was just a test, right?

21:34.543 --> 21:36.586
To see if we lived up to the rumors?

21:38.130 --> 21:40.048
So if you're satisfied with our work,

21:40.132 --> 21:42.718
why don't you tell us
what the real mission is?

21:50.017 --> 21:51.310
Oh, I see.

21:51.852 --> 21:53.478
Sorry for the test.
We had to be sure.

21:53.562 --> 21:56.523
It's no big deal.
Happy to demonstrate.

21:59.234 --> 22:01.236
So that's Abashiri Prison, huh?

22:02.904 --> 22:04.614
We're ready to do whatever it takes

22:04.698 --> 22:06.283
to rescue our comrades.

22:07.242 --> 22:08.327
I understand.

22:12.205 --> 22:13.582
<i>I've finally made it.</i>

22:17.711 --> 22:21.715
<i>I'm here, my friend. My best friend.</i>

22:23.008 --> 22:25.010
<i>I promise I'll rescue you.</i>

22:25.552 --> 22:26.553
<i>Wait for me...</i>

22:27.554 --> 22:28.597
<i>Sakura.</i>
